# bd:envpit-yvyr — verified against the actual mechanism Spring Boot 3.1.3's OWN built-in
# EnvironmentPostProcessors (ConfigDataEnvironmentPostProcessor, SystemEnvironmentPropertySource-
# EnvironmentPostProcessor, etc.) use, by inspecting spring-boot-3.1.3.jar's own
# META-INF/spring.factories directly (`unzip -p spring-boot-3.1.3.jar META-INF/spring.factories`)
# — EnvironmentPostProcessor discovery is STILL spring.factories-based in Boot 3.x (only
# @AutoConfiguration classes moved to META-INF/spring/...AutoConfiguration.imports; this SPI
# did not).
org.springframework.boot.env.EnvironmentPostProcessor=\
com.envpit.spring.EnvpitEnvironmentPostProcessor
